_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":3687,"state":"closed","created_at":"2024-12-19T08:51:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T21:48:38Z","due_on":"2025-09-15T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-06-26T17:29:57Z","updated_at":"2025-06-27T14:44:16Z","closed_at":"2025-06-27T14:44:09Z","assignee":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.5.beta1\n\n### System information\n\nAndroid export\n\n### Issue description\n\nI'm working on the [`sentry-godot`](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-godot) extension, and one of our use cases that we need to support is setting a context for events. Context is basically a dictionary of additional data attached to an error event that is sent to the server. And one of the things that can be a value in a context is an array of different basic data types (so in Godot it corresponds to an untyped Array). We have a bridge layer that facilitates communication between the GDExtension library and the Sentry Android library. The bridge is an Android Plugin library. While implementing contexts for Android platform, I discovered an issue with the generic Arrays being silently ignored when such an array is contained inside a Dictionary and is passed to the Android runtime via Godot's JNI abstractions. I'm not sure if it also affects Java methods that accept Array<Object> – I didn't test it.\n\nI'm preparing a PR to fix this issue.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Define a method in a Godot Android library that accepts a Dictionary parameter:\n```kotlin\n    @UsedByGodot\n    fun testContext(value: Dictionary) {\n        for ((k, v) in value) {\n            Log.v(\"test-godot\", \"key: $k value: $v\")\n        }\n    }\n\n```\n2. On the GDScript side, add an Array to a Dictionary and pass it into that method. \n3. Check the output of `adb logcat -s test-godot`.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nDon't have an MRP at the moment. I can come up with something usable on request.\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.